WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.310
My best friend in high school was Shong.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.650
We would sit together every day at lunch.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.050
Skip classes on Friday's to go on
a weekend adventure and surround

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:24.835
ourselves with way too many snacks when
we were collaborating on our homework.

00:00:24.835 --> 00:00:30.225
Shawn was caring,
mathematically gifted and super cute,

00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:37.792
I've all the girls who would ask me to
deliver a love letters and cards him.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:46.750
However, deep in his heart,
he was depressed.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:52.389
He was deeply upset by his
parent's long time fights.

00:00:52.389 --> 00:00:56.910
He was feeling suffocated
by the unrealistically high

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.470
expectations of his parents.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:05.780
And I, was the only person that he
trusted to share his true feelings with.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.890
One day after school,
I bumped into Shong's mom,

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:15.960
I really wanted to alert her,
to Shong's suffering.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.900
But I was afraid that speaking
the truth would embarrassed her and

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.970
shame Shong, so I remained silent.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.550
After high school, Shong and
I went to different colleges, but

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.340
we stayed in touch.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:41.000
Then, one cold winter night, the second
night after 2014 Chinese New Year,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.680
I received a picture message from Shong.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.630
He had written, happy new year
to me on a frost covered window.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.100
Then I received a call from him.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.810
I picked up and said, thank you so
much Shong, this is so sweet.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:01:59.950
Happy new year to you as well.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.679
But what I heard was Shong
crying uncontrollably.

00:02:10.068 --> 00:02:13.089
He said that he didn't know how
to be happy in the new year.

00:02:15.266 --> 00:02:19.261
He told me that he couldn't
see a way out of his pain, and

00:02:19.261 --> 00:02:22.074
he wanted to terminate his suffering.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:29.475
Before I could respond,
I heard some weird noises.

00:02:31.938 --> 00:02:33.896
And then just silence.

00:02:37.078 --> 00:02:40.504
My heart froze and my mind went blank.

00:02:42.898 --> 00:02:46.381
Shong had jumped out
the window of his dorm.

00:02:50.646 --> 00:02:55.387
I remember how painful it was
waiting outside of Shong's ICU.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:03.060
When I heard Shong's parents condemn
themselves for not recognizing his fragile

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:09.780
mental state, I realized that he had never
spoken to his parents about his suffering.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:12.730
And neither had I.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:20.136
When I had the opportunity,
fear and doubt kept me silent.

00:03:23.721 --> 00:03:30.260
For three days, I fixed my eyes
on Shong's heart monitor screen.

00:03:32.351 --> 00:03:38.204
All of a sudden,
the heartbeat pattern came to a free fall,

00:03:38.204 --> 00:03:41.022
and turned into a flat line.

00:03:44.845 --> 00:03:51.362
I will always remember that
moment of silence when I felt so

00:03:51.362 --> 00:03:58.289
devastated when I realized what
the cost of silence could be.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:07.811
I know this is an extreme case but
perhaps, you can relate,

00:04:07.811 --> 00:04:12.790
perhaps there is being
a time in your life that you

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:17.904
being silent because of
your fear of speaking up.

00:04:17.904 --> 00:04:24.406
I work with friends in a relationship,

00:04:24.406 --> 00:04:31.898
because silence seem
like the safer choice.

00:04:31.898 --> 00:04:37.150
But silence has costs.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.480
When you fail to stand up for
your beliefs,

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.950
you may later feel like you've
lost a part of yourself and

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:49.510
missed out on giving a voice to
others who may feel the same.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:58.470
When you hide a part of your identity for
the fear of not being accepted,

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:05.175
you may suffer from never living fully and
lack a true sense of belonging.

00:05:07.369 --> 00:05:12.602
When you choose not to share your
true feelings with someone you really

00:05:12.602 --> 00:05:18.020
care about, you may miss out on
a potentially beautiful relationship.

00:05:20.492 --> 00:05:28.010
We tend to think that maintaining status
quo is safe while making changes is risky.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:32.922
So we often focus on analyzing
the cost of speaking up

00:05:32.922 --> 00:05:37.398
without even considering
the cost of silence.

00:05:39.665 --> 00:05:46.249
Even I, who have paid such a high
price to understand the cost,

00:05:46.249 --> 00:05:52.725
still found myself being silent
about things that mattered.

00:05:55.283 --> 00:05:58.840
Two years ago, on the outside,
I seemed to have it all.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.145
I was on a promising career track with
the boyfriend who checked all the boxes.

00:06:05.145 --> 00:06:08.715
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And I was living in Hong Kong,

00:06:08.715 --> 00:06:10.255
an exciting new city.

00:06:12.544 --> 00:06:16.110
But the truth was,
I was very unhappy in my job.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:22.870
My boyfriend's critical comments
always made me feel inferior and

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:23.540
never good enough.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.280
And for the first time in my life,

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.300
I was living by myself with
no support group around me.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:38.010
On the inside I felt sad and alone.

00:06:40.508 --> 00:06:44.905
Whenever my parents asked
me how I was doing,

00:06:44.905 --> 00:06:49.545
I wanted to tell them the truth but
I couldn't.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:59.797
I couldn't, because I was afraid to
shutter the illusion of my perfect life.

00:06:59.797 --> 00:07:04.538
I was afraid that something
better didn't exist for me.

00:07:06.531 --> 00:07:13.072
So for nearly a year,
l silenced myself, and it was painful.

00:07:15.025 --> 00:07:22.848
One night, l lay in bed in complete
darkness, l felt hopeless.

00:07:22.848 --> 00:07:24.263
l couldn't see a way out.

00:07:27.303 --> 00:07:31.989
Then suddenly all my memories
of Shong flooding my mind.

00:07:31.989 --> 00:07:36.987
I thought about his
suffering in silence and

00:07:36.987 --> 00:07:41.044
the moment when I lost him forever.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.242
And I was reminded of
the ultimate cost of silence.

00:07:50.893 --> 00:07:56.353
It was at this moment that I
decided to honor Shong's memory by

00:07:56.353 --> 00:08:02.872
breaking my own silence, by taking
the steps that he was not able to take.

00:08:04.575 --> 00:08:07.229
I shared my frustrations and
my fears with my parents.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:13.740
And I was surprised to find that my
being real in front of them felt so

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:17.330
much better than my trying
to be the perfect child.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:25.312
And instead of feeling insecure,
I felt a stronger sense of love and

00:08:25.312 --> 00:08:30.485
belonging by sharing my truth,
rather than hiding it and

00:08:30.485 --> 00:08:33.846
struggling to maintain a illusion.

00:08:36.377 --> 00:08:40.103
With my parents' support,
I end the relationship and

00:08:40.103 --> 00:08:42.155
applied to business school.

00:08:42.155 --> 00:08:45.605
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And look at me now.

00:08:45.605 --> 00:08:50.140
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; This isn't to say that things

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:50.880
are always perfect.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.110
But trust me, they are so much better.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.749
I have found my voice.

00:09:00.225 --> 00:09:06.140
I'm embracing new possibilities and
deeper, more meaningful relationships.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.900
If I had remained silent two years ago,

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:17.749
I will have shut myself off from
everything I'm experiencing now.

00:09:19.951 --> 00:09:23.120
Acknowledging the cost of silence
was a wake up call for me.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.222
I learned it the hard way and

00:09:27.222 --> 00:09:31.686
l don't want you to have to
go through anything similar.

00:09:34.449 --> 00:09:39.336
My greatest hope is that
you can recognize those

00:09:39.336 --> 00:09:44.589
moments when the cost of
speaking up may seem high,

00:09:44.589 --> 00:09:48.756
but the cost of silence is even greater.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:55.437
And that you'll use your
voice to prevent yourself

00:09:55.437 --> 00:09:59.020
from never knowing what might happen.

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.596
How to just spoken up.

00:10:06.745 --> 00:10:08.660
What are you currently being silent about?

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.720
What are you not expressing that might
open up new possibilities for you?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.156
Your relationship with others.

00:10:18.156 --> 00:10:22.203
And perhaps, more importantly,

00:10:22.203 --> 00:10:26.674
in your relationship with yourself.

00:10:29.957 --> 00:10:34.898
I encourage you to find your voice.

00:10:34.898 --> 00:10:35.890
Thank you.

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:39.875
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:10:39.875 --> 00:10:43.909
[MUSIC]

